## 7. Honest Residual

NONE. All 4 Challenger 4 test suites pass in both baseline and double-run modes. The certification gate is real. The previous vacuous contract (only 2 of 4 invoked) was the only real defect, and it is now resolved.

The 4 tests are themselves well-designed:
- test_c4_red7_semantic_subverter.oo: 24 mutants across 4 operator classes, 100% kill rate, plus formal contract anti-vacuity, unconstrained rejection, witness generation
- test_c4_red7_semantic_mutation.oo: 5 laws across 8 DomainCerts, vacuous-input rejection
- test_c4_red8_byzantine_infiltrator.oo: 4 constant-time families (ML-KEM-1024, ML-DSA-87, ChaCha20-Poly1305, HMAC-SHA256) with Dudect |t| < 4.5 bound, RASP Gold Master SHA-256, tamper detection, autonomic rollback
- test_c4_red8_byzantine_active_defense.oo: TLS 1.3, seL4, provable security, ML-KEM-512/768/1024 family, 4 control laws

